@startuml ktop_py_component_architecture
title ktop-py.py Component Architecture

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Single executable file: ktop-py.py" {
  component "CLI parser" as Cli
  component "KtopApp\nTUI state machine" as App
  component "KubectlClient" as Client
  component "DemoClient" as Demo
  component "Snapshot Builder" as Builder
  component "Metrics Loaders\nPrometheus, metrics-server, none" as Metrics
  component "Prometheus Parser" as PromParser
  component "Metrics Server Parser" as MetricsParser
  component "Renderers\nTables, detail pages, CronJobs, charts" as Renderers
  component "Text Viewers\nlogs, describe, YAML" as Viewers
  component "CronJob Analyzer\nschedule, runs, related pods" as CronJobs
  component "Health and Resource Risk\nquotas, limits, scheduler fit, RBAC checks" as Diagnostics
  database "Metric history\nKubectlClient retained samples" as History
}

Cli --> App : parsed args
Cli --> Client : real cluster mode
Cli --> Demo : demo mode
App --> Client : refresh snapshot, logs, describe, YAML, diagnostics
App --> Demo : synthetic snapshot and logs
Client --> Metrics : load_metrics()
Metrics --> PromParser : kubelet/cAdvisor text
Metrics --> MetricsParser : metrics.k8s.io JSON
Metrics --> History : fresh live samples
Client --> Builder : Kubernetes JSON + metrics + history
Demo --> Builder : synthetic Kubernetes JSON + metrics
History --> Builder : retained samples
Builder --> App : ClusterSnapshot
App --> CronJobs : build rows from snapshot workloads
CronJobs --> Renderers : CronJob list and detail
App --> Renderers : overview, details, tables, charts
App --> Viewers : logs, describe, YAML
App --> Diagnostics : health, resource risk, diagnostics

@enduml
